-    TASK:
-    Establish a task-owned, lease-aware sequential runtime handoff for the three
-    mandated local GGUF families. Prove short CUDA generation, clean ownership,
-    process teardown, and VRAM return without killing or attaching to an
-    unowned process.
-
-    CONCRETE STEPS:
-    0. PRECONDITIONS: require two NVIDIA devices, all three cached GGUF files,
-       CUDA-capable llama.cpp bindings, a readable lease ledger, and a writable
-       checkpoint. If a foreign live lease remains, write
-       blocked_lease_aware_gguf_runtime with gate_check_summary and stop.
-    1. Add REQ-INFRA-6973 and tests for lease acquisition, owner identity,
-       stale-ledger discrimination, server ownership, sequential teardown, and
-       bare readiness fields before implementation.
-    2. Declare MODEL_SPECS through cached_sota_pair(gpu_indices=(0, 1)) and
-       require exact IDs unsloth/Qwen3.6-35B-A3B-GGUF,
-       unsloth/gemma-4-31B-it-GGUF, and
-       unsloth/gemma-4-26B-A4B-it-GGUF. Legacy models are smoke-only and cannot
-       set lease_aware_runtime_ready_score.
-    3. Acquire the existing task lease through the shipped ownership API. Record
-       the ledger before and after acquisition, process tree, GPU UUIDs, memory,
-       utilization, model paths, file hashes, and GGUF metadata.
-    4. Load one family at a time in an owned subprocess with n_ctx at least
-       16384 and CUDA offload. Use the embedded GGUF tokenizer, never
-       AutoTokenizer.from_pretrained on the repository ID.
-    5. Generate one fixed nonempty 32-token completion per model. Record actual
-       offloaded layers, GPU memory delta, tokens per second, output hash,
-       exception details, and live duration.
-    6. Close each model and owned subprocess, release its port, and prove both
-       devices return within 512 MiB of the pre-load baseline before continuing.
-       Never kill, reuse, or relabel an unowned server.
-    7. Checkpoint after every model. Set runtime_handoff_complete_score=1 when
-       all model rows are terminal. Set lease_aware_runtime_ready_score=1 only
-       when all three used CUDA, generated output, exited cleanly, released
-       memory, and left a consistent lease ledger.
-    8. Run focused tests, Ruff, OpenSpec coverage, artifact validation,
-       adversarial verification, row-consistency lint, and root-clutter checks.
-    9. REQUIRED ARTIFACT FIELDS: field_principles with one scientific
-       principle per required field and both runtime_handoff_complete_score and
-       lease_aware_runtime_ready_score; preconditions_checked;
-       inference_substrate (live_local_llama_cpp_three_family_lease_owned_cuda);
-       duration_s; live_duration_s; source_artifact_hashes; MODEL_SPECS;
-       models_used; model_file_hashes; gpu_topology; lease_rows;
-       process_ownership_rows; baseline_gpu_memory_rows; load_config_rows;
-       live_generation_rows; gpu_runtime_rows; teardown_rows;
-       vram_release_rows; checkpoint_rows; runtime_handoff_complete_score;
-       lease_aware_runtime_ready_score; random_seed; reproducibility_checksum;
-       gate_check_summary with failed check, expected value, and observed value
-       for any blocked verdict; verifier_is_oracle (false); verdict_class
-       (positive | circular_positive | null | blocked | disqualified | partial);
-       honest_verdict with a terminal prefix consistent with verdict_class.
-
