-    TASK:
-    Build a bounded three-family candidate bank comparing direct,
-    trigger-switched, and draft-conditioned constraint schedules. Keep exact
-    labels and solver feedback hidden during generation, capture raw outputs and
-    adjacent-step energy scalars durably, and do no policy selection here.
-
-    CONCRETE STEPS:
-    0. PRECONDITIONS: require lease_aware_runtime_ready_score=1,
-       fixture_admissibility_ready_score=1, the exact Exp6967 source hash, at
-       least six eligible calibration and six held-out pairs, all model files,
-       two CUDA devices, and a writable checkpoint. On failure, write
-       blocked_delayed_constraint_candidate_bank with gate_check_summary.
-    1. Add REQ-INF-6975 and tests for schedule hashes, balanced pair selection,
-       split isolation, model identity, raw-before-parse durability, energy
-       scalar capture, attempt count, and bare gate fields before implementation.
-    2. Declare MODEL_SPECS through cached_sota_pair(gpu_indices=(0, 1)). Require
-       exact IDs unsloth/Qwen3.6-35B-A3B-GGUF,
-       unsloth/gemma-4-31B-it-GGUF, and
-       unsloth/gemma-4-26B-A4B-it-GGUF. Legacy models may smoke-test only and
-       cannot enter headline rows.
-    3. Before generation, select six calibration and six held-out pairs with
-       two rows per formulation family in each split. Freeze pair IDs, split
-       hash, order, seeds, temperature, top-p, 128-token completion cap, stop
-       rules, and three schedule texts.
-    4. Freeze the schedules: direct ConstraintIR; free reasoning until an
-       unambiguous trigger then a constrained tail; and an unconstrained draft
-       followed by draft-conditioned constrained generation. This is not a
-       finite answer-ID channel and JSON validity is not semantic success.
-    5. Run exactly 12 pairs x 3 schedules x 3 models = 108 live attempts. Use
-       task-owned sequential family processes and batch within a family. Make
-       prompts and raw completions durable before any parse. Checkpoint after
-       each pair block and family teardown.
-    6. Never expose exact witnesses, labels, solver outcomes, held-future rows,
-       or another schedule's result to generation. Keep malformed, empty,
-       truncated, and exception rows.
-    7. Capture only the sufficient adjacent-step statistics for later Spilled
-       Energy recomputation: emitted token ID, selected-token logit,
-       full-vocabulary logsumexp, entropy, top probability, step index, and
-       token-span offsets. Store hashes instead of full vocab vectors.
-    8. Parse after durable capture and record syntax diagnostics only. Do not
-       call Z3, certify semantics, select a schedule, or inspect held-out
-       labels in this task.
-    9. Set candidate_bank_complete_score=1 only when all 108 rows are terminal,
-       all required models used CUDA, schedule hashes match, energy traces are
